{"path":"numeric/math/float_t","title":"float_t, double_t","titleHtml":"float_t, double_t","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/float_t","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"The types float_t and double_t are floating types at least as wide as float and double, respectively, and such that double_t is at least as wide as float_t.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math\"><code>&lt;math.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw1\">typedef</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/* implementation-defined */</span> float_t</span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw1\">typedef</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/* implementation-defined */</span> double_t</span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The types <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span> are floating types at least as wide as <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span></span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>, respectively, and such that <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span> is at least as wide as <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span>. The value of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/types/limits/FLT_EVAL_METHOD\">FLT_EVAL_METHOD</a></span> determines the types of <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> <code>FLT_EVAL_METHOD</code>\n</td>\n<td> Explanation\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span> are equivalent to <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span></span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>, respectively\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"nu0\">1</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td> both <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span> are equivalent to <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"nu0\">2</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td> both <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span> are equivalent to <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">other</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> both <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">float_t</span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">double_t</span> are implementation defined\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;float.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"co2\">#define SHOW(expr) printf(\"%s =&nbsp;%d\\n\", #expr, (int)(expr))</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    SHOW<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/types/limits/FLT_EVAL_METHOD\"><span class=\"kw402\">FLT_EVAL_METHOD</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    SHOW<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">float</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    SHOW<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>float_t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    SHOW<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    SHOW<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>double_t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>FLT_EVAL_METHOD = 1\nsizeof(float) = 4\nsizeof(float_t) = 8\nsizeof(double) = 8\nsizeof(double_t) = 8</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12 Mathematics &lt;math.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12 Mathematics &lt;math.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12 Mathematics &lt;math.h&gt; (p: 231)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12 Mathematics &lt;math.h&gt; (p: 212)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/types/limits/FLT_EVAL_METHOD\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>FLT_EVAL_METHOD</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  specifies in what precision all arithmetic operations are done <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/math","title":"Common mathematical functions"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"float_t, double_t","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. The types float_t and double_t are floating types at least as wide as float and double, respectively, and such that…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"References"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"FLT_EVAL_METHOD","note":"specifies in what precision all arithmetic operations are done"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":188,"codeBlockCount":2}
